{"y":2008,"label":"2007–08","coach":"Jim Calhoun","conf":"Big East","confShort":"Big East","w":24,"l":9,"cw":13,"cl":5,"confFinish":"4th in Big East","finish":"r64","seed":4,"region":"West","apHigh":13,"apFinal":16,"srs":15.54,"sos":6.75,"ortg":110.6,"drtg":98.0,"ppg":77.5,"oppg":68.7,"story":{"headline":"A.J. Price Goes Down, San Diego Stuns","text":"UConn bounced back to 24–9 and 13–5, finishing fourth in the Big East. A.J. Price and Jeff Adrien were first-team All-Big East, Hasheem Thabeet was the league's and the NABC's Defensive Player of the Year, and the Huskies won at No. 7 Indiana and beat ranked Marquette, Pittsburgh and Notre Dame. West Virginia ended their Big East tournament in the quarterfinals, 78–72. As a No. 4 seed in Tampa, UConn lost Price to a torn ACL nine minutes into its first-round game against 13th-seeded San Diego and fell 70–69 in overtime — the first opening-round loss of Calhoun's UConn career. It spoiled a season in which the Huskies went 8–0 at Gampel Pavilion and Price was a USBWA All-American. That May, the coach began treatment for squamous cell carcinoma.","moments":[{"date":"2008-03-21","title":"NCAA First Round: L vs San Diego","text":"UConn lost to San Diego 69–70 (OT) in the NCAA tournament first round at St. Pete Times Forum, Tampa, FL."}],"honors":["Hasheem Thabeet – NABC Defensive Player of the Year","Hasheem Thabeet – Big East Defensive Player of the Year","Jeff Adrien – First-team All-Big East","A.J. Price – First-team All-Big East"],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007%E2%80%9308_Connecticut_Huskies_men's_basketball_team","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UConn_Huskies_men%27s_basketball","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Calhoun","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A._J._Price","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeff_Adrien","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasheem_Thabeet"]},"roster":[{"pid":"jeff-adrien-1","name":"Jeff Adrien","num":"4","cls":"JR","pos":"F","ht":"6-7","wt":243,"home":"Brookline, MA","rsci":"53 ( 2005 )","